WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
28 September 2022.

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.650
Hurricane Ian peaks at
140 knots, category 5.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.070
Then it makes landfall
on Cayo Costa, Florida,

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.710
at 130 knots.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.350
The Saffir-Simpson scale rates
a hurricane by one thing:

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.690
its maximum sustained wind.

7
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:23.110
Yet of the 66 people Ian killed
directly in the United States,

8
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.170
wind accounted for 4.

9
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.370
So if not the wind, what killed
the most people, and why?

10
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.090
In this mission, you'll build a
hurricane from warm water and spin,

11
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.090
and map where and when they form.

12
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.330
Then you'll follow Ian
from Cuba to Florida,

13
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.010
and judge its warnings,
impacts and recovery.

14
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.370
Your mission: explain why water, not wind,

15
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.880
was Ian's deadliest hazard in Florida.
